{
    "background_story": "Hanna was a talented artist who lived in a world of paint-splattered canvases and dusty sketchbooks. Despite being surrounded by the trappings of modern life, she had a confessed aversion to technology. Hanna's friends and family would often tease her about her refusal to own a smartphone, but she couldn't care less. She preferred the tactile feel of a pencil in her hand and the smell of fresh paper. As a result, Hanna's studio was a haven of old-world charm, where the only sounds were the scratching of pencils and the occasional ring of a landline phone. Her technophobic tendencies made her a bit of an anomaly in the digital age, but Hanna wouldn't have it any other way. She believed that the world was already too connected, and that sometimes, the best way to create was to disconnect.",
